t is in them, and 09_Studio_Stage_Rig and WheelSpokes_* are gone.\n4. Car, rig, cameras: mesh hashes, materials and modifiers unchanged. World matrices of all cameras, rig bones, lights and car parts match at frames 1/40/700/1500/2161. 26 cameras, 26 markers, frames 1-2161. My own run of the physics check (lines 1-305 of v5_anim.py, no save): 0 over-limit frames, 0 heading jumps, PASS. The duplicate CAR_LEN/SENSOR_W/lens_for_framing definitions are gone.\n5. Stills: 40 and 1500 look the same. At 700 (Cam_S08_FastPan) there are new translucent vertical bands. I projected the geometry into the camera: they are the now-real fence posts at 64-113 m, motion-blurred by the pan, not stray boxes. This is an expected result of fix 2.\nCosmetic notes, no action needed: action and shader-node names went from Chinese to English because the build ran under --factory-startup; node values and links are otherwise identical. Asphalt and grass use Geometry.Position, which matches the 11/14 film. Flag colours are now seeded, so they may differ from the color film."}}]}
